<main><header class="page-header"><div class="section-inner"><span class="mono-label">Privacy</span><h1>Information with a clear purpose.</h1><p>Last updated 11 November 2026.</p></div></header><article class="section-inner blog-content" style="padding-top:3rem;padding-bottom:6rem">
<h2>MediaHub project briefs</h2><p>When you submit a MediaHub project brief, bapX stores the contact details, organisation, service, budget range, timeline, project description, consent time, and basic source context you provide. Source context can include campaign parameters, referring page, device category, and browser user agent. We use this information to review and respond to the requested engagement and to understand which genuine submissions reach MediaHub.</p>
<h2>What is not a completed lead</h2><p>Opening the form, clicking a call to action, or receiving a validation error is not recorded as a completed MediaHub lead. A completed submission exists only after the server validates and saves the brief.</p>
<h2>Access and sharing</h2><p>Submitted briefs are available only in the authenticated bapX Admin surface to authorised operators. We do not sell project-brief information. We may use service providers needed to host, secure, and operate bapX under appropriate access controls.</p>
<h2>Retention and your choices</h2><p>We keep project briefs only as long as needed for qualification, delivery records, security, and legal obligations. You may ask for access, correction, or deletion by writing to <a href="mailto:hello@bapx.in">hello@bapx.in</a>. Some records may need to be retained where required by law or an active engagement.</p>
<h2>Analytics and advertising</h2><p>The MediaHub form records limited first-party source context with a successful submission. This page does not claim that Meta Pixel, Google Analytics, or advertising cookies are active. If optional third-party tracking is introduced, its consent and disclosure must be updated before use.</p>
</article></main><footer class="page-footer"><div class="section-inner"><span>bapX</span><span>&copy; {new Date().getFullYear()}</span></div></footer></body></html>
